.DS_Store
.venv/
__pycache__/
node_modules/
.pytest_cache/

# Machine-local operator brief for the layout refactor run. The run's own
# committed PLAN.md (§18) is derived from it when the chunks fire.
CLEANUP-PLAN.md

# Local Factory tool state (sessions, caches, local settings). Not evidence.
# Probe and run evidence that should survive is committed under phase-0/evidence/
# instead — see phase-0/evidence/README.md. PRD §9 permits a configured artifact
# path, so nothing here needs to be un-ignored.
.factory/*
!.factory/*.md
!.factory/skills/**

# Skill install paths committed for chunk-11's distribution convention
# (panel-finding G-4 — without an exception these would be gitignored,
# and `test_install_paths_commit_paths_exist` would fail in any clone that
# didn't run the installer). The symlink target `../../../skills/.../SKILL.md`
# lives in this repo's tracked `skills/` dir; the install path itself
# is a thin pointer.
!.factory/skills/**

# Async steering channel for agent runs. Live control input, not part of the record.
STEER.md

# Telemetry rows for §13 efficacy evaluation (PRD §17.3). Schema and aggregator
# live in telemetry/ as committed code; the rows themselves are private data
# and must not enter this repo's git history. aggregate.py reads them from
# $TELEMETRY_DATA_DIR (default ./telemetry) or --data-dir. See
# tools/conventions/model-discipline.md "Migrating the data" for the long-
# term migration gate.
telemetry/runs.jsonl
telemetry/findings.jsonl
telemetry/dispositions.jsonl
telemetry/plan_lint_runs.jsonl

# Sprint-loop runner artefacts (Phase 4.5). The runner writes per-run
# evidence trees to phase-N/build-evidence/<run-id>/; these are runtime
# audit trails, not version-controlled sources-of-truth. Same rationale
# as telemetry rows above — never committed.
# CORRECTED 2026-08-13. The blanket rule below claimed evidence is "never
# committed" while 111 build-evidence files were already tracked (phase-1: 6,
# phase-2: 10, phase-3: 26, phase-3.1: 42, phase-3.2: 6). Ignore rules do not
# apply to tracked files, so the repo silently ran two conventions: phases 1-3.2
# committed their evidence, and from phase-4.5 onward it was dropped — phase-4.5
# has exactly ONE tracked evidence file.
#
# That is worse than a blanket ignore. 111 committed files establish that
# evidence lives here, so the next author reasonably assumes their envelopes are
# captured, and they are not. A rule that fails silently and inconsistently is
# the silent-green shape this project exists to catch.
#
# Policy, stated explicitly: evidence a token or a finding ATTESTS TO must be
# committed — it is the audit trail, and evidence that cannot travel off one
# machine is not evidence (cf. phase-1 F8, where the locked test existed only as
# a hash and is now unrecoverable). Only the runner's per-run scratch trees are
# ignored, and they are matched precisely rather than by directory.
phase-*/build-evidence/r-*/

